{#
  The footer: when this build ran, and what version it claims to be.

  The version comes from settings.yml and falls back to the latest git tag,
  the same order /site.json uses - so the footer and the feed can never
  disagree about which version a reader is looking at.

  The site name and the profile links used to sit here too. The name is in
  the nav on every page and the links are under it, so the footer was
  repeating what was already on screen.
#}
<div class="quirky-footer">
    <p>built {{ build.date }} &middot; {{ settings.version | default(build.version) }}</p>
</div>
